terms.medium_def:
Jacob's son who founded the tribe of Naphtali living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.30.8; 
referred to as Naphtali (נַפְתָּלִי), or Naphtali (KJV= Nephtali) (Νεφθαλείμ); 
son of Israel and Bilhah; 
a brother of Dan; 
half-brother of: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Gad, Asher, Issachar, Zebulun, Dinah, Joseph and Benjamin; 
father of Jahzeel, Guni, Jezer and Shillem.
